Native GoTrue lifecycle suite — can it detect a broken control?
==============================================================

A passing security suite proves nothing unless it can fail (the audit's F-14).
So the F-01 defect is restored on the native-auth database and the same suite
is re-run. It must fail, and fail on the security assertions.

-- restoring the pre-0049 log_password_changed() ---------------------
   restored

-- the suite against the restored defect -----------------------------
✖ [bypass-refused] the retired log_password_changed() is refused to a real session (NOT REFUSED)
✖ [lock-holds-after] and after the attempt the lock is exactly where it was
✖ [no-false-audit] with no audit row claiming a password change
✖ [audit-once] and the change is recorded exactly once
✖ [recovery-cannot-unlock] but a recovery session cannot lift the forced-change lock by any route, and the lock holds
✖ [recovery-reads-nothing] and it reads no records while the account is confined (13)
34 passed, 6 failed

-- re-applying migration 0049 ---------------------------------------
   log_password_changed retired again: t
   callable by authenticated: f

-- and the suite passes again ---------------------------------------

40 passed, 0 failed
